:: cinema.caro.first-meeting -> @exit
  @place-key cinema
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 500
  @when npc.caro.present and npc.caro.schedule.obligationId == "caro_part_time_cinema"
  @when not npc.caro.met
  @onenter
    @effect relationship caro.rapport 1
    @effect set flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered
  @endonenter

  The attendant behind the ticket counter is trying to restock a display of sweets without letting the queue see how precariously the boxes are balanced.

  {{npc.caro.subject | cap}} catches one against {{npc.caro.dependent}} hip, looks up, and gives you a quick, victorious smile. "Caro Novak. Welcome to the glamorous side of the film industry."

  You introduce yourself while {{npc.caro.subject}} straightens the last box. Caro glances towards the programme board, then back to you as if filing your face alongside the week's films.

  @next "Nice save" -> @exit

:: cinema.caro.school-recognition -> @exit
  @place-key cinema
  @auto enter-place
  @priority 500
  @when npc.caro.present and npc.caro.schedule.obligationId == "caro_part_time_cinema"
  @when npc.caro.met and flags.npc.caro.school_encountered and not flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered
  @onenter
    @effect relationship caro.rapport 1
    @effect set flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered
  @endonenter

  The attendant turns from the ticket printer, and you recognise {{npc.caro.object}} before the cinema uniform can make the thought seem unlikely.

  "Nurse Caro?"

  Caro closes {{npc.caro.dependent}} eyes for half a second. "Here I'm just Caro. Preferably Caro-who-is-not-about-to-take-anyone's-temperature." {{npc.caro.subject | cap}} smooths the front of {{npc.caro.dependent}} uniform. "The school pays like it expects gratitude to cover rent. This place pays for the rest."

  {{npc.caro.dependent | cap}} embarrassment gives way to a crooked smile. "Keep my glamorous double life quiet and I might steer you away from the truly awful films."

  @next "Your secret is safe" -> @exit

:: place.cinema
  @hub cinema
  @choices "At the counter"

  Backlit posters line the foyer of {{place.name}}. The smell of popcorn drifts from the concession stand while the screens rumble faintly beyond the ticket barrier.

  @choice "Ask Caro what {{npc.caro.subject}} recommends" -> cinema.caro.recommendation
    @icon 🎬
    @time 5m
    @when npc.caro.present and npc.caro.met and flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered and npc.caro.schedule.obligationId == "caro_part_time_cinema"
  @endchoice

  @choice "Buy popcorn from Caro" -> @exit
    @icon 🍿
    @time 3m
    @when player.money >= 4 and npc.caro.present and npc.caro.met and flags.npc.caro.cinema_encountered and npc.caro.schedule.obligationId == "caro_part_time_cinema"
    @change money -4 "£4 popcorn"
    @response
      Caro fills a striped carton until popcorn forms a dangerously rounded heap above the rim. "Structural integrity is the customer's problem," {{npc.caro.subject}} says, sliding it across the counter.
    @endresponse
  @endchoice

:: cinema.caro.recommendation -> @exit
  @heading "Caro's recommendation"

  Caro folds {{npc.caro.dependent}} arms and studies the programme board with exaggerated seriousness.

  @random
    "Pick the one whose poster tells you the least," {{npc.caro.subject}} decides. "Either it's confident, or the marketing department gave up. Both are interesting."
  @or
    "My professional recommendation is whichever film gets you out before I have to clean screen two," Caro says. "My personal recommendation changes every ten minutes."
  @or
    Caro taps one title on the board. "That one has the fewest complaints so far. I realise that isn't the same as praise, but this uniform demands honesty."
  @endrandom

  @next "Thanks, I think" -> @exit
